From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v8-embed-feedstock <noreply@github.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give abseil the build configuration V8 targets get

v8.gyp opens with

  'includes': ['toolchain.gypi', 'features.gypi'],

and a target_defaults that compiles every V8 target with
-fvisibility=hidden.  abseil.gyp includes only toolchain.gypi and inherits
neither, so abseil alone is built with a different configuration from the
V8 code that includes its headers.  Two consequences, both real:

1. NDEBUG.  It is decided in features.gypi, which abseil.gyp does not
   include, so abseil was compiled without it while every V8 target had it.
   abseil's mutex.h puts Mutex::Dtor inline under NDEBUG and out of line in
   mutex.cc without it, so the symbol was defined twice -- once as a COMDAT
   from v8_libbase, once strongly from abseil:

     abseil.lib(abseil.mutex.obj) : error LNK2005:
       "private: void __cdecl absl::Mutex::Dtor(void)" already defined in
       v8_libbase.lib(v8_libbase.mutex.obj)

   MSVC rejects that outright.  ELF links it anyway, which is worse: the
   ODR violation is silently present in every unix build, with V8's mutexes
   getting the empty inline destructor while abseil's own callers get the
   out-of-line one.

2. Visibility.  Without the target_defaults, abseil was the one part of a
   shared build of V8 compiled at default visibility: 973 exported absl::
   symbols plus the AbslInternal* C entry points, measured on
   libv8.so.14.6.202.34, against 0 for highway and simdutf, which are
   targets inside v8.gyp.  V8's bundled zlib was never at risk because
   Chromium's chromeconf.h renames it to Cr_z_*.

   That matters for an embedder rather than for node.  A process that
   already has an abseil -- conda's libprotobuf pulls one in, built for a
   different C++ standard than V8 uses -- ends up with two implementations
   under identical mangled names, and the dynamic linker binds calls to
   whichever object was loaded first.  The failure is a crash or quiet
   misbehaviour at run time, not a link error.

Including features.gypi fixes the first by construction rather than by
copying a snippet that can drift, and keeps the DEBUG/NDEBUG choice correct
if dcheck_always_on is ever turned on.  The visibility conditions are
v8.gyp's target_defaults ones, verbatim.

After both, the library exports v8::, cppgc::, v8_inspector:: and weak
std:: template instantiations, and nothing else.
---
 tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp b/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp
--- a/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp
+++ b/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp
@@ -1,5 +1,10 @@
 {
-  'includes': ['toolchain.gypi'],
+  # features.gypi as well as toolchain.gypi, exactly as v8.gyp includes
+  # them.  It is where NDEBUG is decided, and abseil's mutex.h puts
+  # Mutex::Dtor inline under NDEBUG and out of line in mutex.cc without
+  # it -- so building abseil with a different answer than the V8 targets
+  # that include its headers defines the symbol twice.
+  'includes': ['toolchain.gypi', 'features.gypi'],
   'targets': [
     {
       'target_name': 'abseil',
@@ -377,6 +382,22 @@
             '<(ABSEIL_ROOT)/absl/time/internal/cctz/src/time_zone_name_win.cc',
           ],
         }],
+        # Same as v8.gyp's target_defaults.  This file is a separate .gyp and
+        # so does not inherit them, which leaves abseil the one part of a
+        # shared build of V8 compiled at default visibility: every absl::
+        # symbol lands in the library's dynamic symbol table, where it can be
+        # interposed with a different abseil in the same process.
+        ['OS=="mac"', {
+          'xcode_settings': {
+            'GCC_SYMBOLS_PRIVATE_EXTERN': 'YES',  # -fvisibility=hidden
+            'GCC_INLINES_ARE_PRIVATE_EXTERN': 'YES',  # -fvisibility-inlines-hidden
+          },
+        }, '(OS!="aix" and OS!="os400") and (OS!="win" or clang==1)', {
+          'cflags': [
+            '-fvisibility=hidden',
+            '-fvisibility-inlines-hidden',
+          ],
+        }],
       ],
     },  # abseil
   ]
